  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Survivors of Modern Slavery in Prisons: The Blind Spot of the UK Anti-slavery Regime</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is conducting research on the policy and legal frameworks relevant to the identification and response to victims of trafficking in prison in the UK. The project will conduct interviews with key stakeholders and survivors of trafficking who have experience of being in prison in the UK. The data and evidence collected will be used to produce a research report. A dissemination event will take place at the end of the project to share the research report and to highlight the key findings and recommendations of the research with relevant stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
